### Page 4 of 7

```text
Annexation – A-11-03 – Stanczyk

Staff Report
November 7, 2011

Page 4

•
Annexation Area – This annexation area contains a 0.62-acre parcel of land described as the
north 170 feet of Tract 6, Briney Tracts. The property contains a house built in 1949 a
detached garage and many mature trees. The property has been completely surrounded by the
City since 1992.
•
Properties to the north – Condominiums
•
Property to the south – Townhomes
•
Properties to the east – Single-family
•
Properties to the west – Townhomes

CURRENT STATUS:  The property contains a single-family home. The purpose of the annexation
is to obtain sewer service for the house.
Improvements: The landowner will be required to comply with Chapter 1.16 of the Cheyenne City
Code, which includes provisions for offsite improvements. Immediate improvements to the property
include installing a sidewalk along the property’s length along Townsend Place. Subsequent
development actions on this property may trigger additional improvements to be made. The property
```

### Page 5 of 7

```text
Annexation – A-11-03 – Stanczyk

Staff Report
November 7, 2011

Page 5

is currently served by City water (BOPU) and is being connected to sanitary sewer. Streets are in
place.
Platting: The property is part of Tract 6, Briney Tracts, platted in 1936.
Zoning:  The property was zoned MR-2 prior to the County’s adoption of new land use regulations
which changed the property to MR.
REVIEWING AGENCY AND REVIEWERS COMMENTS:
City Survey: Site dimensions, legal description and boundary data for this Annexation Map
appear in order.
Engineering: Sidewalk needs to be constructed along Townsend in accordance with City
requirements in conjunction with connection to City water/sewer.  Approximate cost for 120
LF of 6' wide attached sidewalk is $3600, not including any costs of trimming trees or
regrading.  Reconstructing the existing driveway to comply with City standards is also not
included.
Traffic Engineering: 1  The driveway approach on Townsend Place shall conform to the
current regulations.  The minimum and maximum widths and radii for a residential driveway
approach is 10' and 36' and 5' and 10' respectively (ref. Ch. 4, Section 4.3.6, RSSPDS).
2.  The property is adjacent to a street corner.  The property owner is responsible for
installation of sidewalk where none exists on the west side of Townsend Place.  Sidewalk
construction in accordance with current ADA Standards for Accessible Design will be
required (Ordinance, 12.04.200)
Environmental Health: The property is contiguous to the City and is in the 201 Facilities
Management area.  The septic tank shall be properly abandoned and inspected by this office
prior to covering the hole.  If the well is abandoned it shall be done in accordance with State
Groundwater Engineer Standards.
County Planning: Staff supports this annexation and would also support a cooperative plan
to address the annexation of all County pockets.
AGENCIES RESPONDING WITHOUT COMMENT: BOPU, Drainage Engineer, Engineering
Tech/GIS, Fire Department, MPO, Police, County Assessor, County Sheriff, School District,
Cheyenne Light Fuel and Power.
AGENCIES NOT RESPONDING:  Public Works, Bresnan/Optimum, County Fire District #2,
Emergency Management, Laramie County Conservation District, Qwest/Century Link, County
Attorney, County Commissioners, County Public Works.
OTHER COMMENTS RECEIVED:  None
ANNEXATION ELIGIBILITY DATA/ANALYSIS:  Before any territory is eligible for
annexation, the governing body of any city or town, at a hearing as provided in W.S. 15-1-405,
shall find that:
1)
The annexation of the area is for the protection of the health, safety, and welfare of
the persons residing in the area and in the city or town. Findings:  Future required
connections to City services in the Urban Area helps prevent overuse of the aquifer
and possible contamination from septic systems. Urban densities are most
appropriately served by full-time professional fire services and City police.
```

### Page 6 of 7

```text
Annexation – A-11-03 – Stanczyk

Staff Report
November 7, 2011

Page 6

2)
The urban development of the area sought to be annexed constitutes a natural,
geographical, economical, and social part of the annexing city or town. Findings:
The property is 100% contiguous to the existing City boundary. The site is located
within the PlanCheyenne comprehensive plan area, which includes the following land
use designations on the future land use plan: Urban Residential.
3)
The area sought to be annexed is a logical and feasible addition to the annexing city
or town and the extension of basic and other services customarily available to the
residents of the city or town shall, within reason, be available to the area proposed to
be annexed. Findings:  The City has the capacity to serve more people and businesses
with its water and sewer system. This area can be supported by City services, such as
fire protection, police protection, and garbage collection. The proximity to existing
urban development is an opportunity to provide City services in a fiscally responsible
manner.  PlanCheyenne advances urban development in this area and this area is
located in the 201 boundary both of which would require new development to be
connected to City sewer. Sewer service is available at the southern edge of the
property in Townsend. The property already has water service from BOPU.
4)
The area sought to be annexed is contiguous with the annexing city or town, or the
area meets the requirements of W.S. 15-1-407. Findings:  The property is 100%
contiguous with existing City limits.
5)
If the city or town does not own or operate its own electric utility, its governing body
is prepared to issue one (1) or more franchises as necessary to serve the annexed area
pursuant to W.S. 15-1-410. Findings:  Franchises are in place to serve this property.
6)
The annexing city or town, not less than twenty (20) business days prior to the public
hearing required by W.S 15-1-405 (a), has sent by certified mail to all landowners and
affected public utilities within the territory a summary of the proposed annexation
report as required under subsection (c) of this section and notice of the time, date, and
location of the public hearing required by W.S. 15-1-405 (a). Findings:  The required
information was sent September 12, 2011, to meet the requirement of this provision.
ANNEXATION REPORT DATA:  In compliance with 15-1-402 (c) the following information is
provided:
(i)
A map is not required for this report based on the absence of exercising the authority
granted under W.S. 15-3-202 (b) (ii).
(ii)
The total estimated cost of infrastructure improvements required of the landowners by
the City related to the annexation is approximately $3,600.  Additional improvements
may be required with subsequent development actions.
(iii)
Services customarily available to City residents include water, sewer, sanitation,
police and fire protection. Sewer service is available to the property currently; water
lines must be extended to the area in order to obtain City water service. Sanitation,
police and fire services will be available upon annexation. These services are
provided upon application and payment to the Board of Public Utilities, with
sanitation services occurring concurrently.  Provision of these services is initiated by
the property owner.
(iv)
Projected fee for services described in paragraph (iii) (above) is $50 per residence,
per month, and a variable amount for commercial units, based upon volume.
```

